OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30602
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,FForecasts in March and April from
OL,8,FEuropean and US agricultural bodies
OL,9,Fsuggested that UK yields were on
OL,10,Fcourse to be at or above 10-year
OL,11,Faverages in 2026.
OL,13,FBut the latest harvest data from the
OL,14,FAgriculture and Horticulture
OL,15,FDevelopment Board (AHDB) suggests
OL,16,Fwheat, barley and oat yields will all
OL,17,Fbe down, with wheat, around half of
OL,18,Fwhich has been harvested, averaging
OL,19,F6.8 tonnes per hectare, well below the
OL,20,F10-year average.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30603
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,FIf the provisional yield estimates
OL,8,Fhold, the UK cereal and oilseeds
OL,9,Fharvest would be 19.5 million tonnes,
OL,10,Fovertaking 2020 as the worst on record
OL,11,Fsince detailed records began in 1984,
OL,12,Feven after good yields for oilseed
OL,13,Frape, ECIU said.
OL,15,FAnd even if things pick up, 2026 is
OL,16,Flikely to be one of the five worst
OL,17,Fharvests on record ` four of which
OL,18,Fhave occurred this decade, following
OL,19,Fextreme weather made more severe by
OL,20,Fclimate change.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30604
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,FThe UK is battling increasingly
OL,8,Fextreme weather fuelled by climate
OL,9,Fchange, which is mostly caused by
OL,10,Fburning fossil fuels for power, to
OL,11,Ffuel cars, make industrial products
OL,12,Fand heat homes and buildings, along
OL,13,Fwith agriculture and clearing forests.
OL,15,FThis year, the UK has experienced
OL,16,Frecord-breaking deadly heatwaves in
OL,17,FMay and June, followed by heatwaves
OL,18,Fand the driest July on record for
OL,19,FEngland and Wales, plunging the whole
OL,20,Fof Wales and half of England into
OL,21,Fdrought.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30605
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,FThe extremely hot and dry summer comes
OL,8,Fafter a dry spring ` and is the second
OL,9,Fyear in a row of extreme heat and
OL,10,Fdrought, interspersed with extremely
OL,11,Fwet winters in what has been described
OL,12,Fas "weather whiplash".
OL,14,FMartin Lines, chief executive of the
OL,15,FNature Friendly Farming Network (NFFN)
OL,16,Fand a farmer in Cambridgeshire, warned
OL,17,Fthat there was "only so much you can
OL,18,Fdo to adapt to these sort of extremes".
OL,20,FHe said the harvest this year had been
OL,21,F"a real kick in the teeth".
OL,26,@tD@DOUtD@UO]yD@POUzD@fO]}D@AOU}D@ZO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30606
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,F"After two terrible harvests in a row,
OL,8,Fthe crops this year were looking good
OL,9,Fand full of potential coming out of
OL,10,Fspring, only for months of drought and
OL,11,Fheatwaves to destroy any prospect of a
OL,12,Fdecent harvest," he said.
OL,14,F"I've never known it this dry and hot
OL,15,Fon our farm.
OL,26,@oD@AOUtD@PO]vD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30607
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,F"Even farmers I know who were
OL,8,Fsceptical of climate change are now
OL,9,Fsaying they're really worried about
OL,10,Fthe future of their businesses and
OL,11,Fproduction, it's just been completely
OL,12,Fbrutal for our industry."
OL,14,FAnd with high input costs because of
OL,15,Fthe Iran war, he said planning crops
OL,16,Ffor next year was "a total nightmare".
OL,26,@oD@AOUtD@YO]xD@SOUxD@eO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30608
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,F"The nature-friendly practices we've
OL,8,Fdeployed on the farm have helped our
OL,9,Fsoils hold on to water for longer, but
OL,10,Fthere's only so much you can do to
OL,11,Fadapt to these sorts of extremes."
OL,13,FTom Lancaster, land, food and farming
OL,14,Fanalyst at the ECIU think tank, said
OL,15,Fthere was a danger of UK farming
OL,16,Fentering a "climate doom loop", as the
OL,17,Fgreen and pleasant land transformed
OL,18,Finto a "parched and increasingly
OL,19,Funproductive one" in the face of
OL,20,Fextreme conditions.
OL,26,@oD@AOUsD@bO]xD@LOUxD@^O]zD@HOU{D@QO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30609
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,F"At the start of spring farmers were
OL,8,Fhopeful of a better year, but the dry
OL,9,FApril and July and record-breaking
OL,10,Fheat have left farmers facing down the
OL,11,Fbarrel of a third awful harvest in a
OL,12,Frow.
OL,14,F"Farming is now the sector most
OL,15,Fexposed to climate change and the
OL,16,Frisks and damage that it brings.
OL,26,@oD@AOUvD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30610
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,F"From the wettest winter on record in
OL,8,F2024, to the hottest summer in 2025
OL,9,Fand now unprecedented heat and drought
OL,10,Fthis year, we are in danger of UK
OL,11,Ffarming entering a climate doom loop,
OL,12,Fas repeated impacts undermine the
OL,13,Fcapacity of farmers to drill next
OL,14,Fyear's crop," he said.
OL,16,FGlobal temperatures will continue to
OL,17,Frise until emissions of the greenhouse
OL,18,Fgases that are pushing them up are
OL,19,Fbrought down to zero overall ` known
OL,20,Fas net zero.
OL,26,@oD@AOUvD@MO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30611
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,FThat means cutting emissions as much
OL,8,Fas possible by switching to technology
OL,9,Fsuch as wind and solar power, electric
OL,10,Fvehicles and heat pumps, and
OL,11,Foffsetting any remaining pollution by
OL,12,Festablishing forests, restoring
OL,13,Fpeatland and potentially developing
OL,14,Ftechnology to capture carbon from the
OL,15,Fair.
OL,17,FMr Lancaster warned: "Without reducing
OL,18,Femissions to net zero, to bring the
OL,19,Fclimate back into balance, conditions
OL,20,Fwill continue to deteriorate.
OL,26,@yD@VOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,307,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30612
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F306A1785925101
OL,3,C'Brutal' harvest could be worst on
OL,4,Crecord because of extreme summer `
OL,5,Canalysis
OL,7,F"It is now a clear priority for the
OL,8,Ffuture of UK food production, farming
OL,9,Fand the countryside that sustains it."
OL,26,@oD@AOUqD@fO]
